# Beads interactions are an append-only audit log. Merge by RECORD ID, not by
# concatenation.
#
# This line was `merge=union`, added in #4184 to "preserve concurrent entries".
# Union does preserve them — by concatenating both sides of a conflicting hunk.
# When two branches carry the same appended block (routine, since bd re-exports
# the whole file), union keeps BOTH copies. That is how main came to hold one
# 6-record block twice, and 20 duplicate records in total (cave-1poit).
#
# The driver below performs a real union, keyed by record id with the first
# occurrence winning, so a duplicate id cannot survive a merge. Register it
# with `scripts/install-git-hooks.sh` — merge drivers live in git config, which
# is per-clone and cannot be committed.
#
# If it is NOT registered, git falls back to the default text merge: a
# divergent append conflicts loudly instead of silently duplicating. That is
# the correct direction to fail, and `pnpm check:beads-jsonl` catches
# duplicates in CI either way.
#
# issues.jsonl is deliberately NOT routed here: its records are mutable, so
# first-occurrence-wins could keep a stale issue state. A conflict is right.
.beads/interactions.jsonl merge=beads-jsonl
